    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Christian Yelich** (75.84) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (71.03) anchoring the lineup as our most potent options. **Christian Yelich** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against McGreevy, buoyed by a prime leadoff spot and a strong platoon advantage that elevates his floor. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is a high-upside play; despite facing a tougher arm in Kremer, the 16% park factor boost and his leadoff placement make him a vital component for stolen base production, our scarcest category. **Dillon Dingler** (63.90) also presents as a surprisingly strong start, benefiting from his favorable placement in the two-hole and an advantageous matchup against the lefty Springs.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, with **Casey Schmitt** (43.52) narrowly missing the cut. While **Casey Schmitt** held a decent platoon edge against Cease, the high-skill ceiling of the opposing pitcher drove down his efficiency score below our threshold. The primary bench casualty remains **Trea Turner**, who is unavailable today, while **Lars Nootbaar** and **Nelson Velazquez** were excluded due to unfavorable matchups against Harrison and general efficiency concerns. We are carefully monitoring the status of **Yordan Alvarez** (57.36), who faces a difficult same-handed matchup against Griffin; while his xwOBA remains elite, his output is currently suppressed by these situational headwinds, though he retains enough latent value to stay in the starting nine over the remainder of the roster, including **Colt Keith**, **Hyeseong Kim**, or the depth options like **Gary Sanchez**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**.",
